{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To say.</b> Face to face HaShem spoke with you, to say: 'I am,' as was explained above (Exodus 20:1): וַיְדַבֵּר אֱלֹהִים אֵת כָּל הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה לֵאמֹר אָנֹכִי וְכוּ׳ — 'And Elohim spoke all these words, to say: I am…' However, my standing between HaShem and you was in order to tell you the word of HaShem, since you were afraid."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:37.071320522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}